From 3456137f60d7de80740f1d3a39dd41a299955244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:32:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 368/468] RUYI: drm/xe: Synchronize initial DMA mappings on
 noncoherent devices

TTM maps pages write-combined on noncoherent devices. Skipping the CPU
sync on the initial DMA mapping can leave dirty cache lines that later
overwrite data written through that mapping. On EIC7700 with an Arc
A380, this corrupts the GuC firmware before upload.

Only skip the CPU sync on coherent devices.

Signed-off-by: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>

Link: https://github.com/openRuyi-Project/linux/commit/0aee5056860dded5953f5988025fda3e661ceab3
Signed-off-by: Mingcong Bai <jeffbai@aosc.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c
index 29eb4ed576f66..3b5bc62a5daf4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_bo.c
@@ -407,7 +407,7 @@ static int xe_tt_map_sg(struct xe_device *xe, struct ttm_tt *tt)
 
 	xe_tt->sg = &xe_tt->sgt;
 	ret = dma_map_sgtable(xe->drm.dev, xe_tt->sg, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL,
-			      DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC);
+			      xe->ttm.dma_coherent ? DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC : 0);
 	if (ret) {
 		sg_free_table(xe_tt->sg);
 		xe_tt->sg = NULL;
-- 
